2. Statement of modifications (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b))
================================================================================

The scripts in this repository modify Laya checkpoints. Any checkpoint they
produce is a modified derivative of the Apache-2.0 licensed Laya weights, and
carries this statement of what was changed.

2.1 Vocabulary pruning (prune_vocab.py)
    Applied to the laya-multilingual checkpoint (mmBERT-base backbone).
    - The token embedding matrix is sliced from 256,000 rows to the subset of
      tokens a supplied corpus uses, closed over the BPE merge rules so that
      every retained token can still be reassembled from retained parents. The
      reference build for the Zeus robot command set retains 15,188 rows
      (5.9% of the original vocabulary).
    - The tokenizer vocabulary and merge list are rewritten to that subset and
      token ids are remapped accordingly.
    - Transformer encoder and decision head weights are NOT changed. They are
      copied bit for bit from the upstream checkpoint.
    - Consequence: a pruned checkpoint is exact only over the token set it was
      built for. Text outside that set tokenizes differently than it would
      upstream and can therefore decide differently.

2.2 ONNX export (export_onnx.py)
    - The PyTorch module is exported to an ONNX graph with torch.onnx.export
      using the dynamo exporter at opset 18, with dynamic batch and sequence
      dimensions, or with fully static shapes when --pad-to is given.
    - model.encoder.config.reference_compile is set to False before export.
    - The resulting graph is a re-expression of the upstream computation, not a
      retraining or a change of learned parameters.

2.3 Block-wise int8 quantization (quantize_onnx.py)
    - Stale value_info entries are removed from the exported graph, and
      MatMul weights are quantized with MatMulNBitsQuantizer at block_size 64,
      symmetric, 8 bits. Embeddings and the decision head are kept at higher
      precision.
    - Weight values are changed. Decisions produced by a quantized artifact are
      not guaranteed to match the upstream fp32 model.

2.4 What is NOT modified
    - No training, fine-tuning or distillation is performed.
    - The model architecture, the three decision primitives (choice, score,
      noul) and the calibration behaviour are Convai Innovations' work.

